(@ extends 'base-booklet.jtex' @)

(@ block content @)
    \fancypagestyle{instructions}{%
        \pagestyle{naboj}
        \fancyhead[LE,RO]{\textit{(* i18n[language.id].instructions.title *)}}
        \fancyfoot[C]{}
    }
    \pagestyle{instructions}

    \section{(* i18n[language.id].instructions.title *)}
    (# `\protectedInput`, not `\input`, and for the reason `instructions.jtex` carries the same
       note: `evaluators` is an **optional** product -- `modules/naboj/declaration.py` says so,
       and `written()` is what both the builder and the graph read it from -- so this file is
       simply absent wherever a language has not written one. Volume 25 has it in `sk` alone and
       volume 26 in `en` and `sk`, so eight of those twelve `evaluation.pdf` were an
       `Emergency stop` with nothing anywhere naming the missing file.

       Its sibling `answers-modulo.jtex` already reached the same file with `\protectedInput`,
       which is how two templates in one module came to disagree about whether it may be absent.
       `core/tests/test_declarations.py` now checks the rule rather than leaving it to whoever
       writes the next template: a bare `\input` of an optional product is reported. #)
    \protectedInput{build/(* module.id *)/(* competition.id *)/(* volume.id *)/languages/(* language.id *)/evaluators.tex}
(@ endblock @)
